    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "6.2: Info Gap: Two Points",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Pause here so your teacher can review your work. Ask your teacher for a new set of cards and repeat the activity, trading roles with your partner.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "6.2: Info Gap: Two Points",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Here is a graph representing a function of the form \\(h(x) = ab^x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "6.2: Info Gap: Two Points",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Find the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). Show your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A bacteria population starts at 1000 and doubles every 10 hours.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Explain why the expressions \\(1000 \\boldcdot \\left(2^{\\frac{1}{10}}\\right)^h\\) and \\(1000 \\boldcdot 2^{\\frac{h}{10}}\\) both represent the bacteria population after \\(h\\) hours.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "By what factor does the bacteria population grow each hour? Explain how you know.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Equations are helpful for communicating how quantities are changing. We can write equations from descriptions or from graphs.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-026",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes, the information on how a quantity is changing is given in a graph instead of in words. We can find an equation for an exponential function using two points on its graph, just as we’ve done in the past with linear functions.…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-027",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Since the point \\((0,64)\\) is on the graph of \\(f\\), we know the value of the function at 0 is 64. This means that \\(f(0)=a\\boldcdot b^0=a\\), so the value of \\(a\\) is 64.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-028",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Using the second given point, \\((0.5,38.4)\\), we know \\(f(0.5)=38.4\\). This means that \\(64 \\boldcdot b^{0.5}=38.4\\). Solving this equation we have:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-029",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\begin{align} 64 \\boldcdot b^{0.5} &= 38.4 \\\\ b^{0.5} &= \\tfrac{38.4}{64} \\\\ b^{0.5} &= 0.6\\\\ \\end{align}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-030",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "To determine the exact value of \\(b\\), let’s use the properties of exponents. Since \\(b\\) is positive, we can show that \\(b=0.36\\) because",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-031",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\begin{align} b^{0.5} &=0.6\\\\ \\left(b^{0.5}\\right)^2 &= (0.6)^2 \\\\ b &= 0.36 \\end{align}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L06-ACTIVITY-032",
      "SourceSection": "6.3: Bacteria Growth Expressions",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We can now write an equation defining \\(f\\): \\( f(x) = 64 \\boldcdot \\left(0.36\\right)^x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l06.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
